<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5913" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφί-κυρτος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>convex on each side,</i>
			like the moon in her second or third quarter,
				<i>gibbous,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Cael.</u>
				291b20
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>Sign.</u>
				56
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.381d
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>doubly convex,</i> of a curvilinear angle, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφίκοιλος,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Procl.
			</span></i><i>in Euc.Def.</i><i><span class="en">
				8p.127F.
			</span></i>, al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γραμμαί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					2.673
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λεπίδες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					<u>Bel.</u>
					70.23
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
